1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,782
In a primary-care study, more than a third of medicine side effects

2
00:00:03,782 --> 00:00:07,367
that could have been eased went on because the doctor was never told.

3
00:00:07,838 --> 00:00:11,372
Meet Margaret, seventy-eight, on eight medicines, and her

4
00:00:11,372 --> 00:00:13,233
daughter Alex, both fictional.

5
00:00:13,233 --> 00:00:15,713
Urgent care started a new sleeping pill.

6
00:00:16,483 --> 00:00:19,034
Margaret describes her day in her own words.

7
00:00:19,034 --> 00:00:21,933
A clinical language engine reads it on her device.

8
00:00:22,705 --> 00:00:26,388
Woozy becomes dizziness, nearly went over a near-fall, and

9
00:00:26,388 --> 00:00:28,229
no ankle swelling stays a no.

10
00:00:28,229 --> 00:00:31,023
Sofia's fall is set aside as someone else's.

11
00:00:31,023 --> 00:00:33,817
Margaret confirms each answer before saving.

12
00:00:35,571 --> 00:00:39,303
Since lorazepam started, dizziness was recorded on 9 of 14

13
00:00:39,303 --> 00:00:42,134
answered days, compared with 2 of 19 before.

14
00:00:42,134 --> 00:00:45,930
One fall and two near-falls were recorded on those 14 days.

15
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:49,727
It shows a change in what was recorded, not what caused it.

16
00:00:51,769 --> 00:00:56,700
Deterministic code, not AI, checks her eight medicines against AGS Beers

17
00:00:56,700 --> 00:01:01,494
2023, anticholinergic burden, where she scores 7, fall-risk lists, and

18
00:01:01,494 --> 00:01:07,178
possible prescribing cascades, like furosemide for ankle swelling after amlodipine.

19
00:01:07,178 --> 00:01:11,904
Each finding ends in a sourced question for her doctor or pharmacist.

20
00:01:12,682 --> 00:01:16,030
The safety net: here the model's wording failed the source

21
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:19,033
check, so code hides it and the original text stays.

22
00:01:21,151 --> 00:01:27,560
The timeline tests the change in dizziness: Fisher's exact test, p = 0.0023.

23
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:31,101
Falls are listed by date: too few to test.

24
00:01:33,081 --> 00:01:36,654
Ask Kinwise answers from the records: near-falls on 2 of 14

25
00:01:36,654 --> 00:01:38,956
answered days since lorazepam started.

26
00:01:38,956 --> 00:01:42,892
A 3-billion-parameter model running on this laptop's GPU drafts a

27
00:01:42,892 --> 00:01:46,828
plainer answer; code checks every number and medicine name first.

28
00:01:46,828 --> 00:01:50,644
Treatment questions are redirected to her doctor or pharmacist.

29
00:01:52,924 --> 00:01:55,542
The visit brief puts it on one page.

30
00:01:55,542 --> 00:01:59,832
Alex must mark it reviewed before it prints, and it exports

31
00:01:59,832 --> 00:02:02,886
as an HL7 FHIR R4 bundle of 270 resources.

32
00:02:06,491 --> 00:02:11,781
Both test suites rerun live: 94.2 percent micro-F1 on 70 held-out

33
00:02:11,781 --> 00:02:17,641
fictional diary stories, and 57 of 57 synthetic medication cases passed.

34
00:02:18,416 --> 00:02:20,661
Working today: everything you saw.

35
00:02:20,661 --> 00:02:25,813
Partial: the model's code check isn't airtight; no dose or allergy checks yet.

36
00:02:25,813 --> 00:02:30,039
Planned: a validation study, pharmacy import and family sharing.

37
00:02:30,810 --> 00:02:33,344
Kinwise. Records stay in your browser.

38
00:02:33,344 --> 00:02:36,479
Not yet clinician-reviewed; not medical advice.

39
00:02:36,479 --> 00:02:38,413
Try it at the link on screen.
